From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darrel Griet <dgriet@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 20:16:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bluetooth: Clamp accepted LE connection interval floor

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [swift/WCNSS hardware workaround]

The WCNSS Bluetooth controller corrupts its AES-CCM state on an
encrypted LE link when driven at very short connection intervals,
which the peer reports as a MIC failure (HCI 0x3d) and the link is
dropped. This is hit in practice when Android negotiates a 7.5 ms
interval for high-priority GATT (e.g. music remote control).

As the peripheral we answer the LE Remote Connection Parameter
Request with our own le_conn_min_interval as the lower bound instead
of echoing the central's request, so the connection settles on a safe
interval and the encryption engine stays in sync.
---
 net/bluetooth/hci_event.c | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c
index f2c7737e0fac..ddbd9275bc28 100755
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c
@@ -5035,6 +5035,34 @@ static void hci_le_remote_conn_param_req_evt(struct hci_dev *hdev,
 		return send_conn_param_neg_reply(hdev, handle,
 						 HCI_ERROR_INVALID_LL_PARAMS);
 
+	/*
+	 * The WCNSS Bluetooth controller corrupts its AES-CCM encryption
+	 * state -- reported by the peer as a MIC failure (HCI error 0x3d)
+	 * that tears down the link -- when an encrypted LE connection is
+	 * driven at very short connection intervals, e.g. the 7.5 ms that
+	 * Android negotiates for high-priority GATT (music control). As the
+	 * peripheral we cannot forbid an interval outright, but we answer
+	 * the connection parameter request with our own lower bound so the
+	 * central settles on a safe interval instead.
+	 */
+	if (min < hdev->le_conn_min_interval) {
+		/*
+		 * If the whole requested range is below our floor, reject the
+		 * request so the current (safe) connection parameters stay in
+		 * effect. Counter-proposing a longer interval instead makes
+		 * the central re-request every time and the resulting stream
+		 * of interval changes desyncs the link (supervision timeout,
+		 * HCI 0x08). Only raise the lower bound when the requested
+		 * range still leaves room above the floor.
+		 */
+		if (max < hdev->le_conn_min_interval)
+			return send_conn_param_neg_reply(hdev, handle,
+						 HCI_ERROR_INVALID_LL_PARAMS);
+		min = hdev->le_conn_min_interval;
+		if (hci_check_conn_params(min, max, latency, timeout))
+			latency = 0;
+	}
+
 	if (hcon->role == HCI_ROLE_MASTER) {
 		struct hci_conn_params *params;
 		u8 store_hint;
@@ -5060,10 +5088,10 @@ static void hci_le_remote_conn_param_req_evt(struct hci_dev *hdev,
 	}
 
 	cp.handle = ev->handle;
-	cp.interval_min = ev->interval_min;
-	cp.interval_max = ev->interval_max;
-	cp.latency = ev->latency;
-	cp.timeout = ev->timeout;
+	cp.interval_min = cpu_to_le16(min);
+	cp.interval_max = cpu_to_le16(max);
+	cp.latency = cpu_to_le16(latency);
+	cp.timeout = cpu_to_le16(timeout);
 	cp.min_ce_len = 0;
 	cp.max_ce_len = 0;
 
-- 
